{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/249539-new-embeds-please-critique-and-playtest","id":249539,"title":"New Embeds, please Critique and Playtest","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-04T22:17:12-07:00","id":249539,"title":"New Embeds, please Critique and Playtest","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I made few new embeds and I'm curious if they pass muster. If people can evaluate them, and better yet, use them in a game, I would appreciate any feedback.</span><br /> <br /> Cacophony:<br /> Missed Me</span><br /> When a gun is leveled at a target, the destinies of the shooter, the gun and the victim are tied in the moments before the trigger is pulled. This embed creates a mystical feedback loop, forcing the weapon to malfunction instead of injuring the demon. <br /> This can be used on any gun or projectile weapon the demon is touching, or that is pointed at the demon.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Dexterity + Firearms<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant (see designer notes)<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The feedback loop badly malfunctions, fur the duration of the scene, any one using a gun can only fire at the demon, and no one else, until the demon is dead or the scene ends.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> the embed does not work.<br /> <b>Success: </b>The gun jams for a number of rounds equal to the successes rolled, or Primum, whichever is higher.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The gun is completely jammed and cannot be used for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> Design notes:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I designed this embed to get around the fact that Sabotage only works on objects the demon is touching, obvious problem if someone walks through the door with an assault rifle, and work around the fact that once the opposition figures out you\u2019re using Check Background, they start aiming, exactly as the angel in \u201cThe Principal\u201d instructed his minions to do.<br /> As is, this embed is very effective at neutralizing fire arms at a scene, if a robber walk into a bank, he just needs the gunman (or gunmen) to point at the demon are the demon for a second. Useful, versatile, and potentially very powerful.<br /> The other part me wants to make a reflexive action that only takes effect as the weapon is fired, make it damn useful in combat, but not an instant fight stopper. Additionally, it plays into the setting, demons are selfish, good at looking at looking out for themselves, looking out for others takes more effort: if a demon tries to protect someone with this Embed\u2019s second variation, they need to goad the gunman into pointing the gun, and then pulling the trigger, which attracts more attention.<br /> In need community assessment: which version works better balance and fiction-wise?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Instrumental:<br /> Shoot the Moon</span><br /> Angels use the ins and outs of occult physics naturally, instinctively. After Falling, a demon has to relearn these subroutines, often imperfectly. By emulating their former angelic nature, they can boost the effects of another embed, potentially turn a normal success into an exceptional success. This Embed can only be used once in a scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits + Occult<br /> <b>Action: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The demon successfully emulates angelic nature, to the point where the demon now has the Plugged In condition. The God Machine will immediately realize that it has an \u201cangel\u201d in a place where one was not scheduled to be and will start to investigate. <br /> <b>Failure: </b>the embed has no effect.<br /> <b>Success:</b> the demon can add success to those rolled on another embed, if the total successes equals 5 or more it triggers an exceptional success on the original embed. These success do not count for additional effect on the original Embed, only for triggering the exceptional success conditions. If there are not enough total successes to trigger an exceptional success, the embed has no effect and cannot be reused in this scene. <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Any excess successes can be saved, and can be used to turn another embed success into an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Vocal:<br /> Form 44-D</span><br /> Paperwork, paper trails, bureaucracy\u2026 human society depends on it, yet no one pays attention to the mass of scrawled names, numbers and addresses for longer than it take to make sure it\u2019s in order.<br /> It should come as absolutely no surprise that the G-M and its servants use this vast deluge as a control mechanism.<br /> A demon using this embed can create and file a form or closely related series of forms, either in hard copy, electronic copy or both. The form does not cause any action within an organization until someone finds it and acts on it. No one in the organization will remember filling the paperwork, it\u2019s just there, in the system, waiting to be dealt with.<br /> This embed will not cause compromise if it deals with trivial or routine matters: the work order for the third toilet in the men\u2019s bathroom on the fourth floor is beneath notice. If the system is heavily protected (I.e. Adding someone to the FBI\u2019s most wanted list) or if the form in question has some form a human oversight (such as judge signing a warrant), this embed triggers a Compromise roll. If the organization actively <i>avoids</i> oversight there is no Compromise. No demon has, to date, ever had the slightest trouble getting a warrant from the Federal Intelligence Surveillance Court.<br /> Enterprising demons have found that they can fill out personal paperwork in an instant. Being able to fill out your taxes, TPS reports, or PTA form in an minute rather than blow an entire day is a bonus to many. <br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Politics<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The paperwork is badly mishandled in such a way that multiple supervisor become involved. The demon gains the Surveilled condition.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The paperwork did not manifest. The demon will have to find another way to get what he want.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The paperwork manifests as described above. <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The supervisor becomes involved again, but she\u2019s convinced that someone in her organization has screwed up and is going to make sure, personally, that she makes things right with the demon. The demon gain the Connected condition against the organization in question.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Road to Hell</span><br /> \u2026 Is paved with good intentions. Demons are famous for playing on peoples vices, but often a person\u2019s better nature is just as malleable and vulnerable.<br /> Using this the embed a demon can encourage the best in her target\u2019s nature\u2026 usually to achieve her own end.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Manipulation + Empathy- Resolve<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The target in question gives in completely to the worst of his sins. For this scene treat the target\u2019s vice as their virtue. <br /> <b>Failure: </b>the Embed has no effect.<br /> <b>Success: </b>The demon can rewrite one of her target\u2019s most selfish, destructive or cruel aspiration into something positive. A cop\u2019s aspiration to kill a hated criminal could become one to bring him in \u201cby the book\u201d and make sure he faces justices. An abusive parent gains the aspiration to harm his child could become a desire to watch a movie with her.<br /> This effect lasts one scene. During this time the target cannot recover willpower by indulging in their vice. <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The new Aspiration last for a number of days equal to the demon\u2019s Primum. The target cannot recover willpower through his vice during this time.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Shibboleth</span><br /> A Shibboleth is word, pronunciation, inflection or customer that marks a person as a member of an in-group. Americans say \u201ctruck,\u201d Brits say \u201clorry.\u201d <br /> Drawing on this bedrock of custom and story, a demon can move in certain way, talk in a certain way or reference a bit of shared experience that will convince a person or group to accept them as a member of a particular profession or crowd. <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Socialize - highest Intelligence present<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>You\u2019ve tipped of the mark that you\u2019re not what you present your self as. Catastrophically. Roll for compromise.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Embed has no effect.<br /> <b>Success:</b> You convince a person or group present that your \u201cone of us.\u201d The cop at the drug bust believes you\u2019re a plains clothe detective, the construction crew member thinks that you were at the last union meeting, and even the most bilious fanboy won\u2019t call you a \u201cfake\u201d geek girl. In addition, you are +1 for all socialize rolls within that particular \u201cin-group\u201d for the scene, and you add you primum to all social rolls to maintain the illusion of being part of the in-group.<br /> This does not provide additional knowledge or props: you\u2019ll need to use legend if that cop asks to see your ID, and if the union member start debating the merits of proposal 73-C, it\u2019s time to redirect the conversation.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The demon and a member of the in-group hit it off based on their common background. For the duration of the scene one member of the group can act as a one dot Ally or Contact. If demon want to cultivate that person as a long term relationship (and the player spends the necessary XP) she can do so with storyteller permission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T13:02:16-07:00","id":250078,"title":"","content":"Good job. If any of my players take them I'll tell you what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}